'''Space Exploration Technologies Corp.''' ([[doing business as]] '''SpaceX''') is an American [[Space industry|spacecraft manufacturer]], [[space launch]] provider, and a [[Telecommunication|satellite communications]] corporation headquartered in [[Hawthorne, California]]. SpaceX was founded in 2002 by [[Elon Musk]], with the goal of reducing space transportation costs to enable the [[colonization of Mars]]. SpaceX manufactures the [[Falcon 9]] and [[Falcon Heavy]] launch vehicles, [[SpaceX rocket engines|several rocket engines]], [[SpaceX Dragon 2|Cargo Dragon]], crew spacecraft, and [[Starlink]] communications satellites.

SpaceX is developing a satellite internet constellation named [[Starlink]] to provide commercial internet service. In January 2020, the Starlink constellation became the largest satellite constellation ever launched, and as of May 2022 it comprises over 2,400 [[small satellite]]s in orbit.<ref name="sn2676101">{{cite news|last=McDowell|first=Jonathan|date=18 May 2022|title=Starlink Launch Statistics|publisher=planet4589|url=https://planet4589.org/space/stats/star/starstats.html|url-status=live|access-date=18 May 2022|archive-date=21 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210421005810/https://planet4589.org/space/stats/star/starstats.html}}</ref>
The company is also developing [[SpaceX Starship|Starship]], a privately funded, [[Fully-reusable orbital launch vehicle|fully reusable]], [[super heavy-lift launch vehicle|super heavy-lift launch system]] for [[interplanetary spaceflight|interplanetary]] and [[orbital spaceflight]]. Starship is intended to become SpaceX's primary orbital vehicle once operational, supplanting the existing [[Falcon 9]], [[Falcon Heavy]], and [[SpaceX Dragon 2|Dragon]] fleet. Starship will have the highest payload capacity of any orbital rocket ever built on its debut, scheduled for 2022 pending launch license.<ref>{{cite web|date=2022-06-13|title=SpaceX Starship Super Heavy at Boca Chica_FONSI_ROD Final|url=https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/2022-06/20220613%20SpaceX%20Starship%20Super%20Heavy%20at%20Boca%20Chica_FONSI_ROD%20Final.pdf|website=faa.gov|access-date=13 June 2022|archive-date=13 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220613194540/https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/2022-06/20220613%20SpaceX%20Starship%20Super%20Heavy%20at%20Boca%20Chica_FONSI_ROD%20Final.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref>

SpaceX's achievements include the first privately funded [[liquid-propellant rocket]] to reach orbit around Earth,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nasa.gov/offices/c3po/home/spacex_falcon1_flight_4.html |title=SpaceX Successfully Launches Falcon 1 to Orbit |publisher=[[NASA]] |date=September 28, 2008 |access-date=2022-04-29 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110603142912/https://www.nasa.gov/offices/c3po/home/spacex_falcon1_flight_4.html |archive-date=3 June 2011 |url-status=dead}}</ref> the first private company to successfully launch, orbit, and recover a spacecraft, the first private company to send a spacecraft to the International Space Station, the first [[VTVL|vertical take-off and vertical propulsive landing]] for an orbital rocket booster, first reuse of such booster, and the first private company to send astronauts to orbit and to the [[International Space Station]]. SpaceX has flown and landed the Falcon 9 series of rockets [[List of Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy launches|over one hundred times]].

