[[Elon Musk]] published his first [[Tweet (Twitter)|tweet]] on his personal [[Twitter]] account in June 2010,<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Onfro |first=Jillian |last2=Ranj |first2=Brandt |date=January 20, 2022 |title=The very first tweets from famous tech execs like Elon Musk and Marissa Mayer |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/the-first-tweets-of-famous-tech-execs-2013-9 |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160122063411/https://www.businessinsider.com/the-first-tweets-of-famous-tech-execs-2013-9 |archive-date=January 22, 2022 |access-date=April 25, 2022 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref> and had more than 80&nbsp;million followers at the time of the purchase.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Imbert |first=Fred |date=April 4, 2022 |title=Twitter shares close up 27% after Elon Musk takes 9% stake in social media company |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/04/twitter-shares-soar-more-than-25percent-after-elon-musk-takes-9percent-stake-in-social-media-company.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220404102019/https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/04/twitter-shares-soar-more-than-25percent-after-elon-musk-takes-9percent-stake-in-social-media-company.html |archive-date=April 4, 2022 |access-date=April 25, 2022 |publisher=[[CNBC]]}}</ref> In 2017, in response to a tweet suggesting Musk buy [[Twitter Inc.|Twitter]], he replied, "How much is it?"<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mankarious |first=Sarah-Grace |last2=Chacón |first2=Marco |last3=Duffy |first3=Clare |last4=Thorbecke |first4=Catherine |date=April 26, 2022 |title=Here's what Elon Musk has tweeted over the years ... about Twitter |url=https://www.cnn.com/interactive/2022/04/business/elon-musk-tweets-twitter/index.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220427000804/https://www.cnn.com/interactive/2022/04/business/elon-musk-tweets-twitter/index.html |archive-date=April 27, 2022 |access-date=April 27, 2022 |publisher=[[CNN Business]]}}</ref> On March 24, 2022, Musk began tweeting statements critical of Twitter,<ref name="Yahoo" /> polling his followers on whether Twitter adhered to the principle that "[[free speech]] is essential to a functioning democracy".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Duffy |first=Kate |date=April 5, 2022 |title=Elon Musk asks Twitter users whether they'd like an 'edit' button. Twitter's CEO says results of the poll will be 'important.' |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-polls-twitter-edit-button-ceo-agrawal-results-important-2022-4 |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220405095339/https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-polls-twitter-edit-button-ceo-agrawal-results-important-2022-4 |archive-date=April 5, 2022 |access-date=April 25, 2022 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref> Days later, he discussed the future of social media with Twitter co-founder and former CEO [[Jack Dorsey]] and explored the possibility of joining Twitter's [[board of directors]] with [[private equity firm]] [[Silver Lake (investment firm)|Silver Lake]] co-CEO Egon Durban. He relayed this idea to Twitter [[board chair]] [[Bret Taylor]] as well as Twitter CEO [[Parag Agrawal]] on March 27, proposing to either [[Private company|take the company private]] or start a rival social media platform.<ref name="Timeline" />

